I"‹<p>Do you recall a doctor listening to body sounds using a stethoscope? The art of listening to body sounds is called <em>auscultation</em> and dates back to the 1820s. We aim to extract more information from body sounds using signal processing and machine learning, towards remote, cost-effective, and scalable disease screening. We have analyzed respiratory sounds such as breathing, cough and speech collected during the pandemic from individuals with and without COVID-19, and released them openly as the Coswara dataset. Our ANRF-funded project <em>Melodies of the Lungs</em> takes this towards AI-based point-of-care respiratory healthcare.</p>
